    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use the graph of the function to find the indicated values.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="383" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ Find: $$f(0).$$ ⓑ Find: $$f\left( {\frac{1}{2}\pi} \right).$$ ⓒ Find: $$f\left( {- \frac{3}{2}\pi} \right).$$ ⓓ Find the values for x when $$f(x) = 0.$$ ⓔ Find the x-intercepts. ⓕ Find the y-intercepts. ⓖ Find the domain. Write it in interval notation. ⓗ Find the range. Write it in interval notation.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$f(0)=0f(0)=0$$ ⓑ $$f\pi 2=-1f\pi 2=-1$$ ⓒ $$f-3\pi 2=-1f-3\pi 2=-1$$ ⓓ $$f(x)=0f(x)=0$$ for $$x=-2\pi ,-\pi ,0,\pi ,2\pi x=-2\pi ,-\pi ,0,\pi ,2\pi$$ ⓔ $$(-2\pi ,0),(-\pi ,0),(-2\pi ,0),(-\pi ,0),$$ $$(0,0),(\pi ,0),(2\pi ,0)(0,0),(\pi ,0),(2\pi ,0)$$ ⓕ $$0,00,0$$ ⓖ $$(-\infty ,\infty )(-\infty ,\infty )$$ ⓗ $$[-1,1][-1,1]$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
